<Sequential id="uk_10">

  <Vertical id="uk_10_s1" title="Give it back">
    <Chat id="uk_10_give_it_back" src="wool-and-lords.chatpeg" clip="give_it_back"/>
  </Vertical>

  <Vertical id="uk_10_s2" title="The extra permission">
    <Markdown id="uk_10_s2_text">
The envelope left a pale rectangle on the table where the dust had stuck to Zofia's damp sleeve. Niamh put it in her own bag. Zofia nearly reminded her about the attachment. Niamh had already checked it.

Today’s permission covered the supervised Lords visit and a booked room, not their surrendered gallery access. Morwenna counted the visitors, then counted again when Kit came out of the wrong coat.

“That one's mine,” Grace said.

“I wondered why the sleeves had stopped,” Kit said.

Beyond the window, somebody on a bus ate from a paper bag. Zofia wanted five minutes of being that person.

The coat came off. The right coat went on. Their escort opened the next door.

Hale came with Zofia as a voice close to her ear. There was no figure beside the wall. She had brought him from his anchor; he had not been waiting inside for them. Under the voice came the old pressure across her shoulders, the tug towards a departing footstep, the small restless need to return. The animals were still with her too.

She shifted her bag. Nothing shifted the other weight.
    </Markdown>
  </Vertical>

  <Vertical id="uk_10_s3" title="Which House?">
