  <Vertical id="uk_10_s9" title="Repair Kit’s packet">
    <!-- image: alt="Union Flag: St George's red cross, St Andrew's white diagonal cross on blue, St Patrick's red diagonal cross". Checked, licensed teaching asset (license attribute required on the Image); must not imply which flag flies today. -->
    <!-- image: alt="Royal Standard, non-Scottish version: England's three lions in the first and fourth quarters, Scotland's upright lion in the second, Ireland's harp in the third". Checked, licensed teaching asset (license attribute required on the Image); must not imply a flag flies today. -->
    <!-- image: alt="Royal Coat of Arms, non-Scottish version: the shield with a lion and a unicorn as supporters". Checked, licensed teaching asset (license attribute required on the Image). -->
    <Markdown id="uk_10_s9_intro">
Kit has put three teaching images beside his cue sheet. Grace checks their labels aloud.

“Union Flag: St George's red cross, St Andrew's white diagonal cross on blue, St Patrick's red diagonal cross. No Welsh dragon: Wales was part of the Kingdom of England when the flag was designed.”

“Royal Standard: in the version here, England's three lions in the first and fourth quarters, Scotland's upright lion in the second, Ireland's harp in the third.”

“Royal Coat of Arms: the shield has supporters beside it, a lion and a unicorn. That isn't a fourth flag.”

Kit taps the empty cue-sheet pocket. “One packet. Which goes in?”
    </Markdown>
    <CapaProblem id="uk_10_packet" title="Which packet goes in?" dontKnow="true" showanswer="attempted" maxAttempts="1">
      <RulesGrader id="uk_10_packet_grader">
        <StringMatch answer="a" score="1" feedback="Keep this packet. The speech is delivered in the Lords. Introduction hasn't made our Bill an Act. Without carry-over it falls when prorogation ends the session."/>
        <StringMatch answer="b" score="0" feedback="Swap the flag labels. The Union Flag combines crosses; the Royal Standard has quarters with lions and a harp. The supporters identify the arms."/>
        <StringMatch answer="c" score="0" feedback="Keep the image labels; replace the route and Bill note. The speech is in the Lords. An introduced Bill doesn't survive prorogation automatically. Ours has no carry-over arranged."/>
        <Markdown id="uk_10_packet_prompt">**Select one packet.**</Markdown>
        <ChoiceInput id="uk_10_packet_input">
          <Key id="uk_10_packet_a" value="a">A. Union Flag = crosses; Royal Standard = quartered lions and harp; Royal Arms = lion and unicorn supporters. Speech = Lords. Bill = introduced, no carry-over arranged; falls at prorogation, needs reintroduction.</Key>
          <Distractor id="uk_10_packet_b" value="b">B. Union Flag = quartered lions and harp; Royal Standard = crosses; Royal Arms = lion and unicorn supporters. Speech = Lords. Bill = introduced, no carry-over arranged; falls at prorogation, needs reintroduction.</Distractor>
          <Distractor id="uk_10_packet_c" value="c">C. Union Flag = crosses; Royal Standard = quartered lions and harp; Royal Arms = lion and unicorn supporters. Speech = Commons. Bill = introduced, so survives prorogation automatically.</Distractor>
        </ChoiceInput>
        <Explanation id="uk_10_packet_explanation" showWhen="answered">
          <Markdown id="uk_10_packet_explanation_text">
**Packet A goes in.** Union Flag = crosses; Royal Standard = quartered lions and harp; Royal Arms = lion and unicorn supporters. Speech = Lords. Bill = introduced, no carry-over arranged; falls at prorogation, needs reintroduction.

“Keep this packet. The speech is delivered in the Lords. Introduction hasn't made our Bill an Act. Without carry-over it falls when prorogation ends the session.”
          </Markdown>
        </Explanation>
      </RulesGrader>
    </CapaProblem>
  </Vertical>

  <Vertical id="uk_10_s10" title="No second cue" when="@uk_10_packet.correct === correctness.correct || @uk_10_packet.correct === correctness.gaveUp || @uk_10_packet.correct === correctness.incorrect">
